# What this plugin is, for the index in README.md and for whoever installs
# it alone. One key per line, a key repeated for each line of a message;
# ./install.sh at the repository's top installs it from the lines below.
name: xymonapi-agent
version: 0.1.0
side: client
summary: one command that asks an AI agent -- Claude Code, Codex or opencode, headless -- a question about Xymon, with the MCP server as its only tool
requires: xymonapi-mcp >= 0.1.0 (beside it, with xymonapi's client); one of the agent CLIs, installed and logged in; python >= 3.9
manual: xymonapi-agent.1

# How ./install.sh installs it: see xymonapi's PLUGIN file.
needs: xymonapi-mcp
server-files: xymonagent.py xymonapi-agent.sh
server-manual: xymonapi-agent.1
installed: Installed xymonapi-agent beside the API. For /ask: set XYMONAPI_ASK=1 in a file under xymonserver.d/,
installed:   and as the Xymon user install and log in to claude, codex or opencode, then run xymonapi-agent doctor: see xymonapi(8), /ask.
removed: Removed xymonapi-agent. Kept: xymonapi-mcp and xymonapi.
tools-files: xymonagent.py xymonapi-agent.sh
tools-manual: xymonapi-agent.1
command: xymonapi-agent xymonapi-agent.sh
executable: xymonapi-agent.sh
removed-tools: Removed xymonapi-agent. Kept: xymonapi-mcp, xymonapi's client, and its sessions under $XDG_STATE_HOME/xymonapi-agent.
